    ["Why some South Bay patients still come", "People travel north for a sustained tinnitus focus, thorough evaluation, real-ear-verified hearing aids, and Lenire bimodal neuromodulation for suitable candidates. When these matter to you, the drive can be a reasonable trade for specialized care."],
    ["Structuring care around a longer commute", "For South Bay patients we aim to make visits count, investing in a comprehensive first evaluation and spacing follow-ups thoughtfully. Much of a tinnitus plan is carried out at home, so in-person time can stay limited even with a longer trip."],
    ["Prepare before you drive up", "Get oriented from home first. Our [tinnitus knowledge hub](/tinnitus/) and the [why-choose-us page](/tinnitus/why-choose-us/) explain our approach, so your appointment time goes toward your specific tinnitus rather than groundwork you could cover beforehand."],
    ["Do not commute for an emergency", "Urgent symptoms belong close to home and soon. Sudden hearing loss, sudden or one-sided tinnitus, pulsatile tinnitus, or tinnitus with dizziness or neurological symptoms should be evaluated promptly by the nearest appropriate provider, then followed up for management."]
